{% comment %}
  Renders the tax note beneath a price.

  Four audiences share this storefront — NZ trade, NZ retail, AU trade, AU retail —
  and they must not all be told the same thing. Rather than branching on customer
  type, this reads the market's own tax setting through `cart.taxes_included`, so
  the note always states what Shopify is actually doing. Switch a market to
  tax-inclusive pricing in Settings → Taxes and the wording follows on its own,
  with no theme change and no second place to keep in step.

  Trade buyers think and quote in GST-exclusive terms and need no explanation.
  Consumers do, so they are told where the GST appears.

  Accepts:
  - class: {String} extra classes for the wrapper (optional)

  Usage:
  {% render 'price-tax-note' %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  case localization.country.iso_code
    when 'NZ', 'AU'
      assign tax_name = 'GST'
    else
      assign tax_name = 'tax'
  endcase
-%}

<span class="price__tax caption{% if class != blank %} {{ class }}{% endif %}">
  {%- if cart.taxes_included -%}
    Incl. {{ tax_name }}
  {%- elsif customer.b2b? -%}
    Excl. {{ tax_name }}
  {%- else -%}
    Excl. {{ tax_name }} — added at checkout
  {%- endif -%}
</span>
